Subject: [PATCH 0008/0012] draw with OpenGL and keep the decoder's buffers alive

The interface draws with OpenGL, which leaves the video without a Qt Vulkan
device to borrow, so the streamer builds its own buffer-export device (first
graphics queue family, no decode profiles) and Qt never adopts it. The frame
producer then keeps the decoder frame whose descriptor went to the compositor
alive over a one-entry ring: the export already owns its own duplicate of the
handle, and one entry is enough to keep the surface alive until the queued
import and the CPU copy have read it, while leaving the decoder's capture pool
free to recycle. A wider ring pins the pool, which makes the decoder name a
fresh DMA-BUF every frame until the driver refuses one and the immediate buffer
request closes the stream window.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

